==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|frontdoor}}, {{l|en|front-door}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|En-au-front door.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|literal}} The door at the [[main]] [[entrance]] to a [[building]] or [[house]], normally fronts onto a [[street]].
# {{lb|en|by extension}} The entire main entrance to a building or house.
# The habitual or designated main entrance to a room that has more than one door.
#: ''Entry through the toilet's '''front door'''''.
# {{lb|en|computing}} The normal [[portal]] page to a [[website]].
# {{lb|en|baseball}} The path of a [[pitch]] which starts inside and then slides over the [[plate]].
#: ''His '''front door''' slider is hard to handle.''
# {{lb|en|slang}} [[vagina]] or [[penis]], as a means of [[sexual intercourse]], contrasted with the [[anus]] or "[[back door]]"

